  "established_findings":[
    "Unconditional two-step search does not improve the primary metric after RNG isolation and costs roughly 9x compute.",
    "Historical breadth benefits are not transferable without exact executable lineage; benchmark v2 n=48 does not support unconditional width-2 superiority.",
    "Simple breadth thresholds, local-margin depth gates, model-disagreement bonuses, proposal diversification, edge-centric utility replacement, posterior-state gating, calibration correction, variance-reduced EIG racing, and robust maximin EIG across prior classes were falsified prospectively.",
    "Fresh benchmark v2 has frozen executable mechanics, exact 29,281-DAG support, budget 15, strict RNG isolation, and source-addressed lineage.",
    "Fixed graph sparsity priors do not generalize safely across R17-R19; strong coefficient shrinkage, g-priors, scale integration, and predictive family scoring were also prospectively harmful.",
    "S5 identified a useful nonlocal included-effect signal but was unsafe when its posterior controlled planning; S6 falsified simple slab-widening as the remedy.",
    "S7 localized S5's harms to policy feedback: under baseline action replay the nonlocal posterior improved all 12 worlds, mean edge delta -0.638, with zero large harms.",
    "S8 prospectively confirmed dual-posterior separation. Keeping benchmark inference for planning while using the frozen nonlocal posterior only for structural output improved confirmation edge error by 0.470 on average, bootstrap 95% CI [0.316,0.637] improvement, with 22/24 wins, zero large harms, improved mean Brier, and identical actions to control.",
    "Execution reproducibility and namespace isolation remain hard scientific invariants; blocked historical worlds are never pooled."
